#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "aebe3048-cc5b-5340-a15e-d577ae2ee72a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5479" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n![](images/90/901d3a22065b48a8076b9c9aae5563c770c36c9ad40e4063c0f739847e1cda98.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/0c/0c6f9f860a1cf4d510f6c3d4d9c66b77496a354bb1e2cef1b69fd1178e4f15ab.png)\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4\\cdot 3 & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092075 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/id #uuid "55e695b2-4581-5ba7-9604-506234b88323" :question/math-academy-id "e-5480" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n![](images/5c/5ca3e07cfbe9e5d4956b1eab4393601f2a78b0b067d17312e71cbac993e28a86.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/fd/fdbcc62870aefab6214b2f24f53e9bc5654e5386639d4bc328dff3769aff2b45.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation. \n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092076 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/id #uuid "a42d0af8-869c-5c2a-8182-22b14b9546e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5481" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](images/a1/a1b88b7897649bb059cef39d40b2b052a13ac28282223b5688a1bce98296fb53.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿![](images/ca/ca8f02e390e338b62956302ec45ea274ad73a51dafde3fe93b3d1e37dd663699.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-3\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ 70-7\\lambda -10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-17\\lambda +52 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{(-17)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 52}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm 9}{2} \\\\  & =13,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "9e40836e-18e9-5df6-a930-05875b920335" :question/math-academy-id "e-5482" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](images/60/603c59d43e3be000931e7279ac4d27be8aa92692f1528ec57ebd52172affa3cb.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/f9/f91e4886c58db10f60fa666a870aed3c2f456b25e6afb560f857e9c36e81217c.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )-9\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2\\sqrt{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues $\\lambda={\\color{red}3}$ and $\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}.$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix ![](images/aa/aa89b93c6fabd2f3dc7063c85e253ded7482018a5f1c6dadedc74964194c5754.png)\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ad3afc0-1147-5a90-b327-46c419abae45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =7$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402511} {:answer/id #uuid "bebf86c2-9d02-56e0-8de7-e3c093fdb99b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402512} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe3b5b3-5b53-5af3-a386-d1a9cac7570e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402513} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1b2964-fbf6-54e9-a3dc-5eb4004c5b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =7$ and $\\lambda =-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402514} {:answer/id #uuid "00de227b-1e08-5a35-a745-88b3e218426e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fe3b5b3-5b53-5af3-a386-d1a9cac7570e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402513} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c905a94-1e61-56fb-85f0-520ef6a3631a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fda33b2-0f78-5ef6-abce-da9e465c13f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-36780" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(P-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-1\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ 49-7\\lambda -7\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +54 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-14)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 54 \\\\  & =196-216 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $P$ does not have real eigenvalues."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27ca6789-a24a-5ec2-9232-86bc94dc9daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354999} {:answer/id #uuid "2e864f43-7357-599c-9a27-32f22c394e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355067} {:answer/id #uuid "31107606-ccb7-5d05-8596-4e5888c1144b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355094} {:answer/id #uuid "897b443b-8095-5fdd-8fd7-f8556f4d4d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355882} {:answer/id #uuid "bd6f96b4-1d8f-51e8-b377-5e6a706e3f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd6f96b4-1d8f-51e8-b377-5e6a706e3f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356323} :answer-field/id #uuid "44285aea-3536-59ba-a136-9c87d9d92638" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7bbc0e33-82aa-5775-853a-c2bdd5e62b0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-9340" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-7\\cdot 7 & =0 \\\\ 4-2\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-49 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -45 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 45}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{196}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 14}{2} \\\\  & =-5,9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "616d5508-8a25-5988-bb35-0e6edabd52b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355531} {:answer/id #uuid "84cf261d-40c2-521f-8a39-62ae3d4837d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355836} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf397ea-4249-5ec0-9158-e941aa14ba00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356309} {:answer/id #uuid "d61eee99-b39f-5bb9-952c-e406a93f7b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356541} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c54bc1-9006-5edf-ad18-da9b6f40136b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbf397ea-4249-5ec0-9158-e941aa14ba00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356309} :answer-field/id #uuid "e23650fa-a017-55d4-aa2b-e248a6298430" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9a0d751-b8e6-598d-8c36-71f74a16fdfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-9348" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ -2+\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-3,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4.$"}]}
